## 1. Project Overview

**ShiftWeave** is a nursing handoff coordination system built for the **Amazon Alexa+ Developer Hackathon** (Alexa+ Track). It is a multi-turn agentic MCP server that coordinates shift handoffs, task tracking, and nurse-to-nurse handoff synthesis with Alexa voice integration.

### Core Architecture
| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | Node.js / Express (TypeScript) |
| Frontend | React + Vite (TypeScript) |
| MCP Server | Streamable HTTP (`StreamableHTTPServerTransport`) on `/mcp` |
| Database | SQLite (via `SQLITE_DB_PATH`) |
| Reverse Proxy | Caddy 2 (automatic HTTPS) |
| Container | Docker Compose (two services: `app` + `https`) |
| Cloud | AWS EC2 `t4g.medium` ARM64 (Amazon Linux 2023) |
| Registry | AWS ECR (`shiftweave` repo) |
| Config | AWS SSM Parameter Store (`/shiftweave/production/*`) |
| Admin | AWS Systems Manager Session Manager (no SSH) |

