## 7. How to Admin the Server (No SSH)

All server administration is done via **AWS SSM Run Command**:

```powershell
# Step 1: Write command to JSON file (avoids shell escaping hell)
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText("$PWD\ssm-cmd.json", '{"commands":["your command here"]}')

# Step 2: Send command
aws ssm send-command `
  --instance-ids "i-08e66aa7d1bdd0c6c" `
  --document-name "AWS-RunShellScript" `
  --parameters file://ssm-cmd.json `
  --region us-west-2 `
  --output json

# Step 3: Get result (replace CMDID)
Start-Sleep -Seconds 10; aws ssm get-command-invocation `
  --command-id "CMDID" `
  --instance-id "i-08e66aa7d1bdd0c6c" `
  --region us-west-2 `
  --query "{Status:Status,Output:StandardOutputContent,Error:StandardErrorContent}" `
  | Out-File -Encoding utf8 result.log; Get-Content result.log
```

> [!TIP]
> Always use `Out-File -Encoding utf8 result.log; Get-Content result.log` to avoid PowerShell charmap crashes when Docker logs contain emoji characters.

### Common Admin Commands
```bash
# Check container status
docker compose ps

# View app logs
docker logs shiftweave-app-1 2>&1 | tail -30

# View Caddy logs (TLS/cert info)
docker logs shiftweave-https-1 2>&1 | grep -i -E "tls|cert|acme|error"

# Restart everything
cd /mnt/shiftweave && docker compose --env-file .env.deploy up -d --remove-orphans

# Restart only Caddy
cd /mnt/shiftweave && docker compose restart https

# Check .env.deploy
cat /mnt/shiftweave/.env.deploy

# Update .env.deploy value
sed -i 's/^DOMAIN=.*/DOMAIN=newvalue/' /mnt/shiftweave/.env.deploy
```

